### API Gateway Test Collection
### Base URL: http://localhost:5010 (API Gateway)
### All requests route through the API Gateway

@baseUrl = http://localhost:5010
@accessToken = 

### ========================================
### 1. USER SERVICE (via API Gateway)
### ========================================

### 1.1 Register New User (Anonymous - No Auth Required)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "testuser@example.com",
  "password": "Test@1234",
  "fullName": "Test User"
}

### 1.2 Login (Anonymous - No Auth Required)
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "testuser@example.com",
  "password": "Test@1234"
}

### 1.3 Extract Access Token (Run after login)
@accessToken = {{login.response.body.data.accessToken}}

### 1.4 Refresh Token (Anonymous - No Auth Required)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{login.response.body.data.refreshToken}}"
}

### ========================================
### 2. PROJECT SERVICE (via API Gateway)
### ========================================

### 2.1 Get My Projects (Requires JWT)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/projects
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 2.2 Create New Project (Requires JWT)
# @name createProject
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/projects
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "API Gateway Test Project",
  "description": "Testing project creation through API Gateway"
}

### 2.3 Get Project by ID (Requires JWT)
@projectId = {{createProject.response.body.data.id}}
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/projects/{{projectId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### ========================================
### 3. TASKS (via API Gateway → Project Service)
### ========================================

### 3.1 Get Tasks by Project (Requires JWT)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tasks?projectId={{projectId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 3.2 Create New Task (Requires JWT)
# @name createTask
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/tasks
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "projectId": "{{projectId}}",
  "title": "Test task via API Gateway",
  "description": "This task was created through the API Gateway",
  "priority": "High",
  "status": "ToDo",
  "dueDate": "2026-01-15T00:00:00Z"
}

### 3.3 Update Task Status (Requires JWT)
@taskId = {{createTask.response.body.data.id}}
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/tasks/{{taskId}}/status
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": "InProgress"
}

### 3.4 Search Similar Tasks - AI Feature (Requires JWT)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/tasks/search
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "query": "authentication and login implementation",
  "topK": 5,
  "projectId": "{{projectId}}"
}

### ========================================
### 4. COMMENTS (via API Gateway → Project Service)
### ========================================

### 4.1 Get Task Comments (Requires JWT)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tasks/{{taskId}}/comments
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 4.2 Add Comment to Task (Requires JWT)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/tasks/{{taskId}}/comments
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "content": "This is a test comment added through the API Gateway"
}

### ========================================
### 5. FILE SERVICE (via API Gateway)
### ========================================

### 5.1 Get My Files (Requires JWT)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/files/my-files
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 5.2 Upload File (Requires JWT)
# Note: Use Postman or curl for multipart/form-data
# curl -X POST http://localhost:5000/api/files/upload \
#   -H "Authorization: Bearer YOUR_TOKEN" \
#   -F "file=@/path/to/file.txt"

### 5.3 Attach File to Task (Requires JWT)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/tasks/{{taskId}}/attachments
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fileId": "replace-with-actual-file-id"
}

### 5.4 Get Task Attachments (Requires JWT)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tasks/{{taskId}}/attachments
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### ========================================
### 6. AUTHORIZATION TESTS
### ========================================

### 6.1 Test Protected Route WITHOUT Token (Should Return 401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/projects
# No Authorization header - should fail

### 6.2 Test Protected Route WITH Invalid Token (Should Return 401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/projects
Authorization: Bearer invalid-token-here

### 6.3 Test Anonymous Route (Should Work Without Token)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "testuser@example.com",
  "password": "Test@1234"
}

### ========================================
### 7. HEALTH CHECK (If implemented)
### ========================================

### 7.1 API Gateway Health
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

### ========================================
### NOTES:
### ========================================
### 
### 1. All routes starting with /api/auth/** are ANONYMOUS (no JWT required)
### 2. All other routes require JWT Bearer token
### 3. API Gateway validates JWT centrally - no service-level validation needed
### 4. CORS is enabled for http://localhost:3000 (frontend)
### 5. Gateway routes to:
###    - /api/auth/** → user-service:8080
###    - /api/projects/** → project-service:8080
###    - /api/tasks/** → project-service:8080
###    - /api/files/** → file-service:8080
### 
### Expected Responses:
### - 200 OK: Success
### - 201 Created: Resource created
### - 400 Bad Request: Validation error
### - 401 Unauthorized: Missing or invalid JWT
### - 404 Not Found: Resource not found
### - 500 Internal Server Error: Server error
